             "The cabinet had a force-feedback wheel and the game knows nothing about gamepads, so this derives a rumble signal from its own forces and sends it to the pad's motors. XInput controllers only."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_strength_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("100", NULL, 0, 200),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble strength (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_NONE,
             "Scales both motors together; the two below set what each one answers to."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_sustain_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("100", NULL, 0, 200),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: swell (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_NONE,
             "The heavy motor, following the slow half of what the force is doing: the body of a corner, the swell, big undulations."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_impact_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("100", NULL, 0, 200),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: impacts (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_NONE,
             "The light motor, following how fast the force changes: kerbs, walls, chop and landings."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_events",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("true", NULL, 0, 0),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble from the game's own units", ST_BOOL,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_NONE,
             "Takes impacts, terrain and suspension from the game's force-feedback code instead of from the single byte they are summed into. Off falls back to filtering that byte."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_texture_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("50", NULL, 0, 400),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: surface and engine bed (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED, WARNING_NONE,
             "The continuous layer a driver sits on all race: road surface and engine. Boost and nitro have their own control. Trimmed below the impacts on purpose, so a hit still stands out from the ground it happens on."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_texture_curve_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("35", NULL, 2, 100),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: surface range compression (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED, WARNING_NONE,
             "A rough surface can be many times a smooth one, which is wider than two motors can express. Lower compresses that range so tarmac is felt without dirt overwhelming; 100 is no compression."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_boost_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("100", NULL, 0, 200),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: boost and nitro (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_NONE,
             "A spark on both motors when the boost catches, then a buzz on the light motor while it runs. Separate from the surface bed, so trimming the bed does not mute it."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_spring_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("0", NULL, 0, 100),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: add held force back (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_CAUTION,
             "A held force reaches the motors as a drone, so it is removed and only changes are sent. This adds some of it back for a driver who wants the corner present; it is also the one control here that can bring the buzz back."))
SETTING("ffb", "rumble_agc_percent",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("100", NULL, 100, 800),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Rumble: boost quiet stretches to (%)", ST_UINT,
             SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_CAUTION,
             "Scales quiet stretches up against a slowly decaying peak, never down. Off by default: a race trace showed the signal is not quiet, and boosting it pinned both motors at full scale, which reads as one constant buzz."))
/* `rumble_pulse_hz` IS RETIRED AND MUST NOT COME BACK. It chopped the heavy
 * motor at 4..20 Hz to invent road grain, which is a square wave this transport
 * cannot carry: measured 31..110 ms between edges at 8 Hz, where a regular chop
 * would be 62, and aliased to 9.9 Hz at the 20 it accepted. No setting worked,
 * so there was nothing to clamp it to, and the reason it existed stopped being
 * true when ffb_events.c gave the bed the game's own per-tyre jolts. A key left
 * in this file is a key the launcher offers. */
SETTING("ffb", "autocenter",
        STORE_ELSEWHERE("false", NULL, 0, 0),
        SHOW(PAGE_FFB, "Driver autocentre", ST_BOOL, SF_ADVANCED | SF_UNSHIPPED, WARNING_CAUTION,
             "Normally keep this off: it adds a second force to the arcade game's own motor command."))

